# heavy-gate slots: how many heavy jobs may run at once. One whole number from 1 to 8 on a line of its own.
#
# No number here means 3. Lowering it never stops a running job: no new job starts until fewer than the new number hold the gate.
# Every start still passes the memory rules (pressure level 1 or 2 and memory free >= 30%, on two readings 20 seconds apart); those are not set here.
# A value that is 0 or not a whole number is ignored (the default 3 applies, with a warning); a value above 8 counts as 8.
# The file is read on every try, so an edit reaches jobs that are already waiting (on this version of heavy-gate).
# HEAVY_GATE_SLOTS=N in a job's environment overrides this file for that one job.
#
# Edit by hand, or:  heavy-gate slots N     See the number and where it comes from:  heavy-gate slots
# chezmoi creates this file only if it is absent and never overwrites it: your edits stay.
